      "content": "As a general rule, you can only deduct business-related expenses on your tax return. Since the ergonomic chair is for your home studio, it's essential to consider whether it's a home office setup or if it's part of your entertainment or personal area. To qualify as a business expense, the chair should be primarily used for business purposes. If you can show a significant amount of time is spent working in your home studio with that chair, it may qualify as a business expense.",
